Algebra Builder

This game is adapted from Algebra Tiles by teacher.dev (made at the EdTech-a-thon 2026), used under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (the LICENSE file here). The original project's own notices, if any, are kept
with it; this file lists what was changed for Oomba.

Changes made for Oomba (November 2026):
- The look: Oomba's colours, font (Bricolage Grotesque, from the Oomba Kit), rounded cards and buttons.
  The tile colours, the whiteboard layout, the activities, their steps and their checks are unchanged.
- The pages became screens in one self-contained game page (src/App.svelte, src/lib/nav.svelte.ts).
- Sounds and effects come from the Oomba Kit (src/lib/oomba.ts): a passed step, a wrong Check, and the
  finish, which also tells Oomba the problem is complete.
- Activity links and QR codes open the problem on Oomba, written in Oomba's lesson parameters
  (src/lib/oomba.ts); copying goes through the Oomba page.
- Renamed Algebra Builder on Oomba.
- Added question sets (src/pages/SetBuilder.svelte, src/pages/SetPlay.svelte): up to 10 questions from
  any activity, saved on Oomba under a short code, played in order.
- Left out: email links, the "suggest an activity" form, and analytics.
- The math input field is a third-party package, vendored in vendor/mathfield-* under its own terms
  (used with permission), with its package names changed.
- build.mjs makes the bundle pass Oomba's safety scan (no outside addresses, no code built from text).
